\fBpolicy\fR [\fBreport\fR|\:\fBreset\fR] [\fB\-\:top\fR \fIN\fR]
T}	T{
What the listeners in shadow mode would have refused and did not: the count,\: the kind,\: the listener,\: the reason,\: the rule that decided,\: when it was first and last seen,\: and one example of what was asked for,\: most frequent first. \fBreset\fR empties the ledger,\: which is what an operator does after fixing a policy so the next report is about the new one. Shadow mode is \fBpolicy:\: {mode:\: shadow}\fR for the estate or for one listener;\: it covers policy only \-\- authentication,\: bans,\: rate limits,\: bounds and malformed input are refused in shadow mode too
